objective: Expose the source-range-aware caret and range geometry through ui::surface so editor/runtime consumers can use resolved layout geometry without importing private ui::text modules.

implementation:
- zircon_runtime/src/ui/surface/text_geometry.rs: new public surface leaf with text_caret_frame_for_layout and text_range_frames_for_layout.
- zircon_runtime/src/ui/surface/text_geometry.rs: focused regressions cover source-range shaped caret placement and tab fallback to resolved advances.
- zircon_runtime/src/ui/surface/mod.rs: structural module mount and curated public re-export only.
- zircon_runtime/src/ui/text/geometry.rs remains the private geometry owner; no font, raster, renderer, atlas, or IME platform backend policy changed.

focused_tests_added:
- surface_text_caret_frame_uses_source_range_metrics: public surface caret/range API uses shaped source-range width instead of stale per-grapheme advances for simple LTR text.
- surface_text_caret_frame_keeps_tab_resolved_advances: public surface API keeps resolved layout advances for tab text.

